  "problem": "HTML-only crawlers could miss source facts. Sitemap omitted Learn and Methods. Missing records could render a blank details page. Browser-matrix evidence could invent live engine sessions or treat emulators as physical devices.",
  "resulting_behavior": "An HTML-only crawler sees meaningful source content from catalog fields. Unknown data fields are not invented for structured markup. Sitemap includes Methods/guides and eligible source pages. Browser-matrix evidence records actual engines and devices; an emulator is not claimed as a physical-device test. Live Chromium, Firefox and WebKit sessions that were not run remain untested, not passed. Native WebMCP remains untested in unsupported browsers and is distinct from ordinary site usability. No blank detail page or silent stale-context substitution. Six result-card regions remain. plan_research remains disabled. worker/index.mjs does not import enrichment. HTTP 200 is not a completed research task. Last-good generation live-2026-09-03-85b50522b420 is unchanged.",
